From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SP11 audio worker <sp11-audio@localhost>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: qcom: identify speaker diagnostics registration failure

A rejected speaker-protection diagnostics event subscription is currently
reported by the caller as a media format failure. Identify this particular
failure while retaining the error and the fail-closed graph behavior.

This is diagnostic only; it does not establish why the DSP rejected the
registration or authorize bypassing the subscription.
---
 sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/audioreach.c | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/audioreach.c b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/audioreach.c
--- a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/audioreach.c
+++ b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/audioreach.c
@@ -1540,8 +1540,12 @@
 							   PARAM_ID_SP_OP_MODE_NORMAL);
 		if (!rc)
 			rc = audioreach_module_enable(graph, module, true);
-		if (!rc)
+		if (!rc) {
 			rc = audioreach_sp11_register_events(graph, module);
+			if (rc)
+				dev_err(graph->dev, "SP diagnostics event registration failed: %d\n",
+					rc);
+		}
 
 		break;
 	case MODULE_ID_SPEAKER_PROTECTION_VI:
-- 
2.43.0
